- The one real push option is for the job to publish after each rewrite to a hosted realtime service (Pusher or Ably), and for the page to subscribe to it directly. That adds a vendor and a publish step to the job. Since the data changes at most once a minute, push saves at most the 15-second poll interval. I wouldn't take it on unless 15 seconds is too slow.

