Build it in three layers, in this order:

1. **Let the CDN cache `/p`.** Move the cache header out of the app-wide middleware and into the routes. Keep `no-store` on `/account` by scoping it to that router. Leave `X-Frame-Options` and `nosniff` app-wide. Then the products route sets its own policy:

   ```js
   router.get('/:slug', async (req, res) => {
     const product = await db.productBySlug(req.params.slug);
     if (!product) return res.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store').status(404).send('not found');
     const [related, stock] = await Promise.all([
       db.relatedProducts(product.id),
       db.stockFor(product.id),
     ]);
     res.set('Cache-Control', 'public, s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=60');
     res.render('product', { product, related, stock });
   });
   ```

